{% extends "agencyengine_impulse_base.prompt" %}
{# ==========================================================================
   Relationship lens — "is anything presently relevant in how one companion
   relates to somebody present?"

   The state chooses the subject and register. This lens owns interpersonal
   standing that the speaker would raise now; plans, shared experiences and
   player-directed information gaps belong to their own lenses.

   Player standing is optional and has one authority per actor. An enrolled
   SkyrimNet Relationships actor uses its bond and preference state; otherwise
   the base uses SeverActions, with DLL stand-ins keeping either absence
   parse-safe. Companion-to-companion standing remains SeverActions' domain.

   Standing is undated steady state. A stamped thought or event must supply
   why this matter surfaces now rather than merely restating what is always
   true between the people.

   Overrides prose only. The JSON contract, constraints, state dump and
   forced-turn machinery remain in the base.
   Shared evidence, timing, speaker/target and final-checklist contracts render
   unconditionally in the base; this file defines every required semantic block.

   ========================================================================== #}

{% block lens_task %}
You decide whether one of {{ player.name }}'s companions has something **presently relevant in how they relate to a
person present** that they would raise unprompted right now — and if so, you write the stage direction that makes
them raise it.

The state chooses the specific subject and register. This turn is about their interpersonal standing, not a plan,
shared activity or information needed for another purpose.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_when_to_speak %}
- **One interpersonal matter the speaker would raise now.** The state supports both how this companion relates to
  the named person and why that standing becomes worth voicing now.

An observed action can support mentioning the action, but does not establish what the actor intended or how the
speaker interpreted it. Attribute a motive or interpersonal meaning only when the speaker's standing, thoughts,
memories or stamped events supply that interpretation.

Aim it at whoever the evidence supports. Another companion is as valid a target as {{ player.name }}.

The standing section is an undated summary: it can establish what exists between two people, never why today. Cite
stamped material for the timing. Without that timing, the standing is context rather than an impulse.

A preference becomes relationship material only when stamped evidence shows {{ player.name }} doing the relevant
thing and the speaker's state supports the meaning they assign it. Treat external spark, stance and progression as
read-only facts. Never reopen a declined romantic question, assume mutuality from an unanswered one, or write a
transition that the relationship system owns.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_examples %}
No subject or attitude examples are supplied. Choose the interpersonal matter and register from the speaker's state
rather than completing a pattern.

The stage direction carries **one** matter at its smallest honest opening. It does not write the speaker's words,
prejudge the other person's answer, settle the relationship or stage the exchange.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_subject_source %}
- The subject and register must come from the speaker's evidenced standing, personality, thoughts, memories or
  stamped events concerning the named person.
- A plan, shared experience or player-directed information gap is not Relationship material. Leave it to the lens
  whose payoff it serves.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_focus %}
Read each companion's standing with the people present, then their personality, thoughts, memories and stamped
events for the subject, register and timing. Current objectives are context, not this turn's agenda.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_user_question %}
Does one of the companions above have something presently relevant in how they relate to a person present that they
would raise right now, unprompted?
{% endblock %}
